.TH VITALS 1 "2026-09-13" "vitals 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vitals \- your system's vitals, all at a glance
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vitals
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vitals
is a system information tool (the fastfetch / neofetch class) with 61 modules.
.PP
It shells out for nothing: it reads
.IR /proc ,
.IR /sys ,
.IR /etc
and uses system calls directly. Zero subprocesses, zero
.BR unsafe ,
writes no files, sends no network packets. Every line it prints can be questioned
about where it came from —
.B \-\-sources
prints the files each module
.B actually
read, recorded at runtime rather than kept as a hand-written list.
.PP
With no options it renders whatever the config file says; a config file replaces the
built-in default view outright.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Config file to use. Without it,
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vitals/config.toml
then
.I $HOME/.config/vitals/config.toml
are tried; if neither exists the built-in default is used. Naming a file that does not
exist is an error (exit code 1); a missing default path silently falls back.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output JSON (turns off colors and the logo). Shape:
.IR docs/json.md ;
schema:
.IR docs/vitals.schema.json .
.TP
.BI \-\-logo " auto|none|NAME"
Logo:
.B auto
picks one by distribution (the default),
.B none
hides it, or name one directly. Names are case-insensitive, and an unknown name falls
back to the generic art instead of failing.
.TP
.BI \-\-module " LIST"
Show only these modules, comma-separated. The order is yours, and a module the config
does not list can still be named.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Turn colors off; same as setting
.BR NO_COLOR .
.TP
.B \-\-list\-modules
List every available module (61 of them).
.TP
.B \-\-gen\-config
Print the built-in default config to stdout, comments included.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Write diagnostics (including the effective settings) to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Explain, module by module, why each one appeared or did not — shown, empty, skipped,
failed, each with its own reason. It speaks about the
.B result
and therefore really collects once.
.TP
.B \-\-sources
Print the files each module
.B actually
read. Given both this and
.BR \-\-explain ,
state is printed first, then evidence.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH MODULES
There are 61 modules;
.B vitals \-\-list\-modules
lists them and the repository file
.IR docs/modules.md
documents each one, including the files it reads. The reference has an English edition,
.IR docs/modules.en.md .
.PP
Broad groups: system 13 (os, host, kernel, bios, board, chassis, uptime, datetime,
version, init\-system, bootmgr, processes, loadavg); hardware 21; session and desktop 16;
network and throughput 6; software 2 (packages, rust); layout 3 (title, separator, break).
.PP
Four of them — net\-io, disk\-io, cpu\-usage, top — are differential: each waits out a
200 ms sampling window. They collect in parallel, so the total is about one window.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config file is TOML, and TOML is the only format supported. It
.B replaces
the built-in default view: once it lists
.BR modules ,
the built-in list is gone.
.PP
Each module may carry conditions; when one is not satisfied the module is skipped, and a
skip is not an error (the exit code is still 0):
.B when\-file\-exists
(a path exists),
.B when\-command\-exists
(a same-named file is found along
.BR PATH ,
the command is
.B never
executed) and
.BR platforms .
Several conditions are combined with AND.
.PP
Example configs live in
.IR presets/ .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VITALS_LANG
Help language, \fBzh\fR or \fBen\fR. Without it the locale decides
.RB ( LC_ALL ,
.BR LC_MESSAGES ,
.BR LANG )
and anything unclear means Chinese. Runtime messages (\fB\-\-explain\fR,
.BR \-\-sources ,
errors) are currently Chinese only; the help is bilingual.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turn colors off (same as
.BR \-\-no\-color ).
.TP
.B CLICOLOR_FORCE
Force color even when stdout is not a terminal.
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Terminal width; it decides whether the logo is drawn beside the fields.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " HOME
Where the config file is looked up.
.TP
.B PATH
Used by
.B when\-command\-exists
for lookup only — never executed.
.TP
.BR LC_ALL ", " LC_CTYPE ", " LANG
The locale module, and some formatting.
.TP
.BR TZ ", " TZDIR
Time zone. Zone names are validated as paths, and relative names containing
.B ..
components are refused.
.PP
Several modules read further variables of their own
.RB ( SHELL ,
.BR USER ,
.BR LOGNAME ,
.BR VISUAL ,
.BR EDITOR ,
.BR XCURSOR_* ,
.BR TERM* ,
.BR XDG_* );
the full list is in
.IR docs/cli.md .
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Normal, including
.BR \-\-explain ,
.BR \-\-sources ,
.BR \-\-list\-modules ,
.B \-\-gen\-config
and "one module failed to collect but the rest rendered fine". A module failure only
warns on stderr and never invalidates the other modules' output.
.TP
.B 1
Config read, parse or version error; or a write failure.
.TP
.B 2
Argument error (unknown option, unknown module, extra positional argument).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/vitals/config.toml
User config.
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Distribution information. Use
.B \-\-sources
for the complete per-module list.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
The default view:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
vitals
.EE
.RE
.PP
Just a few modules:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
vitals \-\-module os,cpu,memory
.EE
.RE
.PP
For scripts:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
vitals \-\-json | jq \-r '.entries[] | "\\(.key): \\(.value)"'
.EE
.RE
.PP
Ask where a line came from, and why a module is missing:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
vitals \-\-sources \-\-module os,host
vitals \-\-explain \-\-module os,gamepad
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use an example config:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
vitals \-\-config presets/headless.toml
.EE
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
The repository's
.IR docs/
directory:
.BR modules.md ,
.BR configuration.md ,
.BR cli.md ,
.BR json.md ,
.BR faq.md ,
.BR logo.md ,
each with an English
.B .en.md
edition. Security audit:
.IR AUDIT.md
(Chinese).
